{
  "id": "lib-modifier-hooks",
  "order": 9,
  "title": "Modifier hooks",
  "goal": "Port `modifiers/hook` (armor, behavior, build, combat, interaction, mining, ranged, special): the hook interfaces a modifier module can implement and the code that asks every modifier of a tool in priority order (`ModifierHooks`, `ModuleHook`, the merging of the answers). In Rust each hook is a trait the modules implement, and a dispatcher takes a tool's modifiers (from the model in lib-tool-nbt) and calls the hook on each. Keep the signatures plain: a context struct for what the game provides, no game types.",
